  "06-01": ["James 1:5", "If any of you lack wisdom, let him ask of God, that giveth to all men liberally, and upbraideth not; and it shall be given him."],
  "06-02": ["Proverbs 2:6", "For the LORD giveth wisdom: out of his mouth cometh knowledge and understanding."],
  "06-03": ["Proverbs 4:7", "Wisdom is the principal thing; therefore get wisdom: and with all thy getting get understanding."],
  "06-04": ["Proverbs 9:10", "The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom: and the knowledge of the Holy One is understanding."],
  "06-05": ["Proverbs 11:14", "Where no counsel is, the people fall: but in the multitude of counsellors there is safety."],
  "06-06": ["Proverbs 15:22", "Without counsel purposes are disappointed: but in the multitude of counsellors they are established."],
  "06-07": ["Proverbs 12:15", "The way of a fool is right in his own eyes: but he that hearkeneth unto counsel is wise."],
  "06-08": ["Proverbs 19:20", "Hear counsel, and receive instruction, that thou mayest be wise in thy latter end."],
  "06-09": ["Proverbs 18:15", "The heart of the prudent getteth knowledge; and the ear of the wise seeketh knowledge."],
  "06-10": ["Proverbs 16:16", "How much better is it to get wisdom than gold! and to get understanding rather to be chosen than silver!"],
  "06-11": ["Proverbs 3:13", "Happy is the man that findeth wisdom, and the man that getteth understanding."],
  "06-12": ["Proverbs 8:11", "For wisdom is better than rubies; and all the things that may be desired are not to be compared to it."],
  "06-13": ["Proverbs 14:8", "The wisdom of the prudent is to understand his way: but the folly of fools is deceit."],
  "06-14": ["Proverbs 10:14", "Wise men lay up knowledge: but the mouth of the foolish is near destruction."],
  "06-15": ["Proverbs 24:3–4", "Through wisdom is an house builded; and by understanding it is established: And by knowledge shall the chambers be filled with all precious and pleasant riches."],
  "06-16": ["Proverbs 20:5", "Counsel in the heart of man is like deep water; but a man of understanding will draw it out."],
  "06-17": ["Ecclesiastes 7:12", "For wisdom is a defence, and money is a defence: but the excellency of knowledge is, that wisdom giveth life to them that have it."],
  "06-18": ["Proverbs 1:5", "A wise man will hear, and will increase learning; and a man of understanding shall attain unto wise counsels:"],
  "06-19": ["Proverbs 2:10–11", "When wisdom entereth into thine heart, and knowledge is pleasant unto thy soul; Discretion shall preserve thee, understanding shall keep thee:"],
  "06-20": ["Proverbs 3:21", "My son, let not them depart from thine eyes: keep sound wisdom and discretion:"],
  "06-21": ["Proverbs 22:3", "A prudent man foreseeth the evil, and hideth himself: but the simple pass on, and are punished."],
  "06-22": ["Proverbs 14:29", "He that is slow to wrath is of great understanding: but he that is hasty of spirit exalteth folly."],
  "06-23": ["Proverbs 17:24", "Wisdom is before him that hath understanding; but the eyes of a fool are in the ends of the earth."],
  "06-24": ["Proverbs 4:5", "Get wisdom, get understanding: forget it not; neither decline from the words of my mouth."],
  "06-25": ["Psalm 90:12", "So teach us to number our days, that we may apply our hearts unto wisdom."],
  "06-26": ["Colossians 4:5", "Walk in wisdom toward them that are without, redeeming the time."],
  "06-27": ["James 3:17", "But the wisdom that is from above is first pure, then peaceable, gentle, and easy to be intreated, full of mercy and good fruits, without partiality, and without hypocrisy."],
  "06-28": ["1 Kings 3:9", "Give therefore thy servant an understanding heart to judge thy people, that I may discern between good and bad: for who is able to judge this thy so great a people?"],
  "06-29": ["Proverbs 28:26", "He that trusteth in his own heart is a fool: but whoso walketh wisely, he shall be delivered."],
  "06-30": ["Proverbs 1:7", "The fear of the LORD is the beginning of knowledge: but fools despise wisdom and instruction."],
